/*
RMSTEST_25 - cross-shaped land placement area
preview-design.md Sec.15 item 2

QUESTION
Where can a neutral land origin actually land. Guide:803 says "lands are
positioned at random in a cross-shaped area, and will never be in the corners"
and gives no numbers. Sec.6.1 approximates that as rejecting a candidate when
both |x-center| and |y-center| exceed dim*0.35, which is a guess nobody has
tested. The 0.35 was never measured.

METHOD
Sixty single-tile neutral lands of SNOW, no land_position, so every origin is
sampled by the engine's own rejection loop. Each land is then one 4-connected
SNOW patch and its centroid is the origin. Read the scatter, not a screenshot.

min_placement_distance 0 on every land, and every land left in the shared
default zone, so neither origin spacing nor other_zone_avoidance_distance
shapes the scatter. The only surviving constraint is the cross.

GENERATE AT TINY (120). Center is 60. Under the 0.35 model the rejected corner
region is the four 18x18 squares beyond 42 tiles from center on BOTH axes,
which is 1296 of 14400 tiles, or 9 percent. Sixty origins over five runs is 300
samples, so a uniform draw would put about 27 in those corners and the cross
model predicts zero. The two are far apart enough to separate in one sitting.

PREDICTIONS, RECORDED BEFORE THE RUN
1. Zero origins in the four corner squares. If any appear, 0.35 is too small.
2. If the true boundary is looser than 0.35, origins appear in a ring inside
   the corner squares and the innermost corner origin gives the real constant
   directly, as max(|x-60|, |y-60|) over the corner-most sample.
3. The scatter is symmetric about both axes. An asymmetric result means the
   cross is not centered, which nothing in the guide suggests.

READ IT WITH
  python probe_scenario.py "<scenario>" --patches SNOW

WATCH FOR, and this is the failure mode that does not announce itself
The patch count must be 60. Two origins landing within one tile merge into a
single patch, and a merged patch reports one centroid sitting between two real
origins, which is a plausible-looking coordinate that is not an origin. A patch
of roughly 20 tiles where the rest are roughly 10 is the tell. Discard any run
whose patch count is below 60 rather than trying to correct it.
*/

<PLAYER_SETUP>
  random_placement

<LAND_GENERATION>
  base_terrain GRASS

  create_land { terrain_type SNOW number_of_tiles 1 base_size 1 min_placement_distance 0 }
  create_land { terrain_type SNOW number_of_tiles 1 base_size 1 min_placement_distance 0 }
